Z||000003||artherd||08-17-2001||10:27 AM||||you want just about any cadilac after 1994.  Reportedly some of the 1993 motors had head gasket issues that were fixed in 94 and later.<P>PS: the 01 northstar has a slightly lowered compression (10.0:1 instead of previous 10.3:1) to run 87 octane, but it also gets fordged connecting rods.<P>Personally, I'd go for a 94-97 engine if you plan to use the stock ECU (in 98 they changed to OBD-II systems which are a pain.)<P>Hope this helps!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
